course: dictionary
lesson: 3239
title: Environmental
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Animals shed skin and slime into water, so testing a cup of lake water can show which fish, frogs or rare animals live there; this is called environmental DNA.» Environmental is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you what kind of DNA this is: the kind that comes from the natural world, here the water and animals in a lake.
explain: Look for clues around the word. The sentence is about water, fish, frogs and rare animals, so environmental is about nature. In science and geography lessons it often goes with pollution, climate change, recycling and protecting wildlife, as in «environmental problems» and «environmental group».
explain: Environmental can also mean the surroundings around someone, such as the noise or light in a place. If a bedroom has loud traffic and bright streetlights all night, its environmental conditions make sleeping hard. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "about the surroundings" fits, you have it.
fact: Environmental means about the natural world: air, water, land, plants and animals, and how people affect them.
fact: Environmental can also mean about the surroundings or conditions around someone, like noise or light.
fact: «Environmental damage» means harm done to nature.
fact: «Environmental issues» are problems that affect nature, such as pollution.
fact: «Environmentally friendly» means causing little harm to nature.
exercise: In «environmental DNA», what does environmental describe? | the bottom of a swimming pool | *the natural world, such as the water and animals in a lake | a type of cake | a game played indoors
exercise: Mia's class started an environmental group to clean up the park. What kind of group is it? | a group that cooks food for the school fair | a group that practises a dance | *a group that cares about nature and how people affect it
exercise: Which word fits best? The bedroom had loud traffic and bright streetlights all night, so its ___ conditions made sleeping hard. | famished | musical | *environmental | ancient
test: Which phrase is about nature? | reading corner | birthday party | school dinner menu | *environmental problems
test: Dad says the new shop uses paper bags, so it is environmentally friendly. What does that mean? | *It causes little harm to nature | It costs the most money | It is open all night | It is a shop that sells sweets
exam: Which two meanings does environmental have? | Only plants and animals | Only the weather | *The natural world, and the surroundings or conditions around someone | Only sounds
